<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Desk view — {{ book }} — run {{ run_id }}</title>
<style>
 :root{--bg:#fbfaf7;--fg:#1c1b19;--muted:#6b6862;--line:#e4e1da;--ok:#1f7a4d;--okbg:#e6f4ec;--bad:#b3261e;--badbg:#fbe9e7;--warn:#8a5a00;--warnbg:#fff3d6;--stale:#4b4f57;--stalebg:#e9eaee;--mono:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace}
 body{margin:0;padding:24px 20px 60px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:14px/1.45 -apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:1240px;margin-inline:auto}
 h1{font-size:22px;margin:0 0 2px}.sub{color:var(--muted)}.line{font-size:16px;margin:10px 0 18px}
 table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);font-size:13px}th,td{padding:7px 9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;text-align:left}th{background:#f3f1ec;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}
 .mono{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px}.num{text-align:right;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap}
 .st{display:inline-block;border-radius:4px;padding:2px 8px;font-weight:700;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.2px}
 .st-MISMATCH{background:var(--badbg);color:var(--bad)}.st-DISAGREEMENT{background:var(--warnbg);color:var(--warn)}.st-ATTESTED{background:var(--okbg);color:var(--ok)}.st-STALE{background:var(--stalebg);color:var(--stale)}
 tr.r-MISMATCH td{background:#fff8f7}tr.r-STALE td{background:#f6f6f8}
 .why{margin-top:3px;color:#333}.why a{color:inherit}
 details{margin-top:28px}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)}
 .wrap{overflow-x:auto}.ind{color:var(--muted);font-size:11px}
 /* evidence modal (inline script, no framework) */
 #backdrop{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(20,18,15,.45);display:none;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:center;padding:40px 16px;overflow:auto;z-index:10}
 #backdrop.open{display:flex}
 #modal{background:#fff;color:var(--fg);border-radius:10px;max-width:1040px;width:100%;box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.35);padding:18px 22px 22px;position:relative}
 #modal h2{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:18px}#modal .close{position:absolute;top:10px;right:14px;border:0;background:none;font-size:22px;cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)}
 #modal table{font-size:12.5px}#modal td.f{font-family:var(--mono);white-space:nowrap}
 #modal .cite{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;background:#f6f4ef;border-left:3px solid #cfc9bd;padding:3px 8px;margin:3px 0;white-space:pre-wrap}
 #modal .q{border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:4px solid var(--bad);padding:8px 10px;margin:6px 0;border-radius:4px;font-size:13px}
 #modal details{margin-top:14px}#modal summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
 #modal .cons{color:var(--bad);font-weight:600}
</style></head><body>
<h1>{{ book }}</h1>
<div class="sub">6am page · run {{ run_id }} · {{ ts }}</div>
<div class="line"><b>{{ exposure.total|musd }}</b> gross delta-equivalent exposure under check<span class="ind"> (indicative)</span> across <b>{{ rows|length }} positions</b> · <b style="color:var(--ok)">{{ exposure.attested|musd }} attested</b> ({{ n_attested }}) · <b style="color:var(--bad)">{{ exposure.attention|musd }} requires attention</b> ({{ n_attention }}){% if n_stale %} · <b style="color:var(--stale)">{{ exposure.stale|musd }} stale</b> ({{ n_stale }}){% endif %}</div>
<div class="sub">The red figure is the delta exposure of positions whose booking does not match the document or whose reading is uncertain: until the booking is corrected, no risk number from that position can be trusted. It is the position's delta, not the delta attributable to the discrepancy; attributing it would mean repricing booked versus documented terms, which this system does not do (roadmap: hedge-to-liability coherence). Rows requiring attention are sorted by delta exposure, largest first; their Δ USD is shown in red. Booked notional in the book: {{ exposure.notional_total|musd }} (USD-equivalent, indicative FX).</div>
<div class="wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>reference</th><th>product</th><th>underlying</th><th class="num">notional</th><th>maturity / expiry</th><th class="num">Δ<span class="ind"> (% notional)</span></th><th class="num">Δ USD-equiv.<span class="ind"> (indicative)</span></th><th class="num">vega<span class="ind"> ($/vol pt)</span></th><th>trust</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in rows %}
<tr class="r-{{ r.state }}"><td class="mono"><a href="run_report.html#{{ r.doc_id }}">{{ r.trade_id }}</a></td><td>{{ r.product }}</td><td class="mono">{{ r.underlying }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.notional }}</td><td class="mono">{{ r.maturity }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.delta }}</td><td class="num"{% if r.state != 'ATTESTED' %} style="font-weight:700;color:var(--bad)"{% endif %}>{{ r.delta_usd_fmt }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.vega }}</td>
<td><span class="st st-{{ r.state }}">{{ r.state }}</span><div class="why">{{ r.why }} <a href="run_report.html#{{ r.doc_id }}" class="ev" data-doc="{{ r.doc_id }}">→ evidence</a></div></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="ind">Risk figures (delta, delta USD-equivalent, vega, FX) are indicative fixtures for the demo book and are not computed by this system. Convention: the delta of the booked position from the desk's side (the desk sold the call and issued the note, so both are short the index); the hedge is the mirror image and is not shown. The trust column asserts direction of concern, never magnitude. Trust states: ATTESTED — booking attested against the document, both model families agree on every field; DISAGREEMENT — reading uncertain, human review queued; MISMATCH — documented and booked terms differ; STALE — a prior attestation no longer applies because the document or booking changed since.</p>
<details><summary>Behind the scenes: the agent's tools on this run (call counts from the trace, nothing inflated)</summary>
<div class="wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>tool</th><th>kind</th><th class="num">calls</th><th>notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for t in tools %}<tr><td class="mono">{{ t.name }}</td><td>{{ t.kind }}</td><td class="num">{{ t.calls }}</td><td>{{ t.note }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="sub">Cost of this check: <b>${{ '%.2f'|format(cost) }}</b> for {{ rows|length }} documents (${{ '%.2f'|format(cost / (rows|length if rows|length else 1)) }} per document), traced tokens × list prices; the marginal cost per additional position is flat. Models extract and explain; code decides. Full evidence per position in <a href="run_report.html">run_report.html</a>; quality numbers in eval_report.md.</p>
</details>

<div id="backdrop" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"><div id="modal"><button class="close" aria-label="close">×</button><div id="modal-body"></div></div></div>
<script id="evidence" type="application/json">{{ evidence_json|safe }}</script>
<script>
(function(){
  var data = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('evidence').textContent);
  var bd = document.getElementById('backdrop'), body = document.getElementById('modal-body');
  function esc(s){ return String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, function(c){ return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;'}[c]; }); }
  function row(f){
    var cites = f.citations.map(function(c){ return '<div class="cite">“' + esc(c) + '”</div>'; }).join('');
    var cons = f.consequence ? '<div class="cons">' + esc(f.consequence) + '</div>' : '';
    var det = f.type !== 'CLEAN' ? '<div class="sub">' + esc(f.detail) + '</div>' : '';
    return '<tr><td class="f">' + esc(f.field) + '</td><td class="t-' + esc(f.type) + '">' + esc(f.type) + '</td><td>' + esc(f.severity) + '</td>'
         + '<td class="mono">' + esc(f.ts) + '</td><td class="mono">' + esc(f.bk) + '</td><td>' + cons + det + cites + '</td></tr>';
  }
  function open(doc){
    var d = data[doc]; if (!d) return;
    var bad = d.findings.filter(function(f){ return f.type !== 'CLEAN'; }), ok = d.findings.filter(function(f){ return f.type === 'CLEAN'; });
    var head = '<tr><th>field</th><th>type</th><th>sev</th><th>documented</th><th>booked</th><th>consequence · citations (both families)</th></tr>';
    var html = '<h2>' + esc(d.trade_id) + ' <span class="st st-' + (d.lane === 'AUTO_CLEAR' ? 'ATTESTED' : 'MISMATCH') + '">' + esc(d.lane) + '</span></h2>'
      + '<div class="sub">' + esc(d.product) + ' · source ' + esc(d.source || 'txt') + (d.parse ? ' · parse job ' + esc(d.parse) : '') + ' · <a href="run_report.html#' + esc(doc) + '">full run report ↗</a></div>';
    if (bad.length) {
      html += '<h3 style="margin:12px 0 6px;font-size:14px">' + bad.length + ' finding' + (bad.length > 1 ? 's' : '') + ' requiring attention</h3><div class="wrap"><table><thead>' + head + '</thead><tbody>' + bad.map(row).join('') + '</tbody></table></div>';
      var qs = bad.filter(function(f){ return f.triage; });
      if (qs.length) html += '<h3 style="margin:14px 0 4px;font-size:14px">Drafted desk queries</h3>' + qs.map(function(f){ return '<div class="q"><b>' + esc(f.field) + '</b> · ' + esc(f.classification || '') + '<br>' + esc(f.triage) + '</div>'; }).join('');
    } else {
      html += '<p>No findings requiring attention: every field agrees across both families and matches the booking.</p>';
    }
    html += '<details><summary>' + ok.length + ' field' + (ok.length !== 1 ? 's' : '') + ' CLEAN (auto-cleared with citations)</summary><div class="wrap"><table><thead>' + head + '</thead><tbody>' + ok.map(row).join('') + '</tbody></table></div></details>';
    body.innerHTML = html; bd.classList.add('open'); document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  }
  function close(){ bd.classList.remove('open'); document.body.style.overflow = ''; }
  document.querySelectorAll('a.ev').forEach(function(a){ a.addEventListener('click', function(e){ e.preventDefault(); open(a.getAttribute('data-doc')); }); });
  bd.addEventListener('click', function(e){ if (e.target === bd) close(); });
  document.querySelector('#modal .close').addEventListener('click', close);
  document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){ if (e.key === 'Escape') close(); });
})();
</script>
</body></html>
